@@ -1,6 +1,23 @@
 ## Build libs
 Run `BuildFidelityFXDX11.bat` from the `sdk` folder. Compiled libs are located in `sdk\bin`.
 
+For 32-bit Windows applications, run `sdk\BuildFidelityFXDX11_x86.bat`.
+This selects the Win32 target, uses `sdk\build-x86`, and builds the DX11 backend,
+FSR1, FSR2, FSR3 upscaler, FSR3, optical flow and frame interpolation host libraries.
+The bundled shader compiler still requires a 64-bit Windows build host. Shader
+bytecode is independent of the CPU target architecture. CMake, Visual Studio C++
+tools with Win32 support and a Windows SDK must be installed.
+
+To include the hardware smoke test, pass `-DFFX_DX11_SMOKE_TEST=ON`. After building,
+run `sdk\build-x86\Release\ffx_dx11_smoke.exe`. It checks backend context lifecycle,
+dispatches three FSR3 upscaler frames and reads back the output. The test requires
+a D3D11 hardware device with feature level 11.1 for the FSR3 shader UAV bindings.
+It does not test frame generation, swap-chain integration or the sample applications.
+Use the SDK CMake project directly; the root sample project still targets x64.
+Consumers must also target Win32, use matching SDK headers and match Debug/Release
+and CRT settings. RelWithDebInfo uses the same library names as Release and the
+script builds it last, so it replaces the Release libraries in `sdk\bin\ffx_sdk`.
+
 <h1>Welcome to the FidelityFX Super Resolution 3 SDK</h1>
 
 ![alt text](/docs/media/fidelityfxsdk-logo-rescaled.png)
